lt a complete real-time message board application with:\\n\\n**Backend (server/):**\\n- Express server on port 3001 with CORS and JSON parsing\\n- Embedded PGLite database persisted to `server/pglite-data/` directory\\n- `messages` table with `id`, `text`, `created_at` columns\\n- `GET /api/messages` — fetch all historical messages\\n- `POST /api/messages` — insert new message, return it, broadcast via SSE\\n- `GET /api/stream` — SSE endpoint maintaining active client connections and broadcasting new messages\\n\\n**Frontend (client/):**\\n- Vite dev server on port 5173 with `/api` proxy to backend\\n- Vanilla JS SPA with HTML form input + message list display\\n- Fetches initial message history on page load\\n- Connects to SSE stream via `EventSource` for real-time updates\\n- Form submission posts to backend and clears input\\n\\n**Root (app/):**\\n- `concurrently` runs both dev servers with single `npm run dev` command\\n- No manual setup needed — PGLite data directory auto-created on first run\\n\\nAll checklist items from the spec are implemented: project initialization, backend infrastructure, database setup, SSE real-time capabilities, and frontend implementation.\"}"}}]}
